//===----------------------------------------------------------------------===//
// The relation: "what the consumer reads on the device is what the producer
// wrote on the host." It relates two values -- the buffer before the copy and
// the buffer after it -- across a host->device launch, the one boundary no
// amount of inlining can remove.
//
// A relaxed cross-device copy omits the release, so the device may observe a
// stale buffer. Nothing in the kernel shows this: the parameter looks the same
// either way. It is the classic heterogeneous-offload bug, and it is silent.
//
// Vx turns the consumer's requirement into a boundary obligation and discharges
// it at the seam with z3. The `assert` inside the spawn is the contract; the
// pre-scan carries it back to the transfer that produced the buffer, and the
// solver is asked whether the post-copy state can violate it. `unsat` accepts,
// `sat` rejects with the counterexample.
//
// Run (needs z3 on PATH; seam verification is off by default):
//   vxc www/book/src/correlation/04_freshness_across_the_launch.vx --verify-seams
//
// Expected:
//   Error[E6004]: relaxed transfer of 'a' across the CPUDRAM -> NPUHBM seam
//   violates the boundary contract: the buffer carries no synchronizing
//   release, so a consumer may read it stale
//   note: z3 counterexample: ((tag_a #b11) (val_a #x0000000000000000))
//
// Change `.to_device_relaxed()` to `.to_device()` and the same obligation is
// discharged `unsat` and the program is admitted.
//
//===----------------------------------------------------------------------===//

fn stage(a: Tensor<i32, [4]>) -> i32 {
  // The `_relaxed` variant is the escape hatch: it drops the release, and with
  // it the visibility guarantee the consumer below depends on.
  let local_a = a.to_device_relaxed();
  spawn on(Topology::NPU[0]) {
    // The contract. It is what the seam obligation is asked to preserve.
    assert(local_a[0] == 42);
  };
  return 0;
}

fn main() -> i32 {
  let t = Tensor<i32, [4]>::uninit();
  return stage(t);
}
